  "question": {
    "text": "The order of increasing sizes of atomic radii among the elements O, $\\mathrm{S}$, Se and As is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BAS4X",
      "text": "\nAs $ < \\mathrm{S} < \\mathrm{O} < \\mathrm{Se}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "S5j6L",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Se} < \\mathrm{S} < \\mathrm{As} < \\mathrm{O}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PluSh",
      "text": "\nO $ < $ S $ < $ As $ < \\mathrm{Se}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Y1a81",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O} < \\mathrm{S} < \\mathrm{Se} < \\mathrm{As}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "On moving down in a group atomic radii increases due to successive addition of extra shell hence\n$$\n\\mathrm{O} < \\mathrm{S} < \\text { Se }\n$$\nFurther As is in group 15 having one less electron in its $p$ orbital hence have higher atomic radii than group 16 elements.\ni.e., $\\mathrm{O} < \\mathrm{S} < \\mathrm{Se} < \\mathrm{As}$",
    "image": null
  },
